          path: build/Build/Products/Debug-iphonesimulator/MyApp.app

  visual-regression:
    needs: build
    runs-on: macos-15
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
OVERVIEW: Provision, inspect, and tear down managed simulators.

USAGE: grantiva simulator <subcommand>

OPTIONS:
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

SUBCOMMANDS:
  ensure                  Create or reuse a named simulator and boot it.
                          `--name` alone reuses an existing simulator with that
                          name. To create one, the name must contain a device
                          model ("iPhone 17") or --device-type must be given;
                          the newest installed runtime is used unless --runtime
                          is passed.
  delete                  Explicitly delete a named simulator.
  sessions                List Grantiva-managed simulator capacity slots.
  teardown                End a managed session, or reclaim one simulator by
                          UDID when no ledger entry exists.
  cleanup                 Delete Grantiva-created simulators that are shut down
                          and not part of an active session.

  See 'grantiva help simulator <subcommand>' for detailed help.
OVERVIEW: Explicitly delete a named simulator.

USAGE: grantiva simulator delete [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet] --name <name>

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --name <name>           Name of the simulator to delete.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

OVERVIEW: List Grantiva-managed simulator capacity slots.

USAGE: grantiva simulator sessions [--json] [--verbose] [--quiet]

OPTIONS:
  --json                  Output as JSON
  --verbose               Print diagnostic detail (timestamps, labels,
                          metadata) to stderr.
  --quiet                 Silence progress diagnostics on stderr; warnings and
                          errors still print. Program output on stdout is
                          unaffected.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

